    <section class="guide-section" id="how-to">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">07 &mdash; Production</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to create good Tech UGC</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Lead with the problem, not the product</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Show the product interface within 5 seconds</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">End with a concrete result the viewer can relate to</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The Tech UGC script structure</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Hook (0&ndash;3s).</strong> State a relatable problem or a surprising outcome. "I used to spend 3 hours editing videos. Now it takes 10 minutes." The hook must be specific and concrete &mdash; vague hooks like "This app is amazing" don't work for tech.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Problem context (3&ndash;8s).</strong> Briefly establish the pain point. What was the old way? Why was it frustrating? One or two sentences maximum.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Product demo (8&ndash;25s).</strong> Show the product working. This is the core of Tech UGC. Screen recording, app walkthrough, or prompt-to-output demo. The viewer must see the interface and understand the workflow.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Result (25&ndash;30s).</strong> Show the concrete outcome. "I wrote a 2,000-word article in 15 minutes." "My studying time dropped by 40%." The result must be specific and relatable.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>CTA (final 2&ndash;3s).</strong> Simple and direct. "Link in bio." "Try it free." Do not oversell &mdash; the demo already did the selling.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Common mistakes in Tech UGC</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Too much talking, not enough showing</strong> &mdash; the product interface should appear within 5 seconds. Don't spend 15 seconds on a talking head before showing the screen.</li>
          <li><strong>Feature listing instead of workflow demonstration</strong> &mdash; "It has AI writing, templates, and collaboration" is worse than showing one complete workflow end to end.</li>
          <li><strong>Vague hooks</strong> &mdash; "This app changed my life" doesn't work for tech. Use specific numbers: "I built a landing page in 7 minutes using AI."</li>
          <li><strong>Too long</strong> &mdash; 15&ndash;45 seconds is the sweet spot. Tech UGC needs to be tight. Every second that doesn't teach something loses viewers.</li>
          <li><strong>No concrete result</strong> &mdash; always end with a measurable outcome the viewer can relate to.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Equipment for Tech UGC</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A modern smartphone, a screen recording tool (built into iOS and Android), and a free editing app (CapCut, in-app editors). For voiceover content, a quiet room matters more than an expensive microphone. Most top Tech UGC creators produce entirely on their phone.</p>
